; Original pressure-dependent-demand civil hydraulic verification case.
; SI input: LPS flows, metres elevations/lengths/pressure heads, millimetres diameter.
; Reference results are generated independently by WNTR 1.5.0 / EPANET 2.2.
[TITLE]
Deficient-head pressure-dependent demand with exponent 0.5

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID Elevation RequestedDemand
J 0 10

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID Head
R 10

[PIPES]
;ID Node1 Node2 Length Diameter Roughness MinorLoss Status
RJ R J 1000 100 130 0 OPEN

[OPTIONS]
UNITS LPS
HEADLOSS H-W
DEMAND MODEL PDA
MINIMUM PRESSURE 0
REQUIRED PRESSURE 20
PRESSURE EXPONENT 0.5
SPECIFIC GRAVITY 1
VISCOSITY 1
TRIALS 200
ACCURACY 0.000001
UNBALANCED STOP
DEMAND MULTIPLIER 1

[TIMES]
DURATION 0
HYDRAULIC TIMESTEP 1:00
PATTERN TIMESTEP 1:00
REPORT TIMESTEP 1:00
REPORT START 0:00

[REPORT]
STATUS YES
SUMMARY YES
NODES ALL
LINKS ALL

[COORDINATES]
R 0 0
J 1000 0

[END]
